            "review_title": "Review at Quan Ngon Thai (SAWASDEE)",
            "review_text": "thebillet\nLincolnshire43 contributions\n1\nVery competent Thai cuisine\nApr 2018 • Couples\nWe visited as a family for dinner and as a couple for lunch. The location is just a couple of minutes stroll from Hanoi Rock City and other expat haunts. It over looks a small lake adjacent to West Lake. The views from the back are very nice.\n\n Inside there is a front dining room which fronts the road while the back room overlooks the lake. The decor is natural and tidy. The menu is full of the famous Thai dishes one might expect from a simple and unpretentious restaurant. Prices are very competitive. \n\nThe quality of the food was good but careful on your spice rating, they can produce very spicy dishes, just ask for little spice and that matches what we've had in Thailand and UK. \n\nStaff were extremely pleasant and helpful.\nOverall a good quality competitively priced lunch and dinner option.\nRead more\nWritten April 23, 2018",
